# Prisma ORM Rules (v6.16+ - 2025)

## What's New in Prisma ORM (2025)

### Rust-free Architecture (v6.16.0 - September 2025)
- **90% Smaller Bundle**: Reduced from ~14MB to 1.6MB
- **3.4x Faster Queries**: New TypeScript Query Compiler
- **No Native Binaries**: Simplified deployment and platform flexibility
- **Lower CPU Footprint**: More efficient query execution
- **ESM-first**: Modern ES modules support

### General Availability Features
- **omit API**: Most requested feature - exclude fields from queries
- **Multi-schema Support**: Native multi-schema PostgreSQL support
- **JSON/Enum in SQLite**: Better SQLite type support
- **updateManyAndReturn**: Bulk updates with returned data
- **Auto-generated ULIDs**: Alternative to UUIDs
- **Sharding Support**: @shardKey for PlanetScale sharding

### Developer Experience
- **VS Code Database UI**: Visual database management
- **GitHub Copilot Extension**: Fast documentation lookups
- **Agent Mode**: Help with migrations and database workflows
- **Prisma Postgres**: Local database instances by default
- **Ask AI**: Integrated AI assistance in Prisma Console
- **2x Faster Migrations**: Optimized shadow database interactions

## Installation & Setup

### Install Prisma
```bash
npm install prisma @prisma/client
npx prisma init
```

### Prisma Schema (schema.prisma)
```prisma
// schema.prisma
generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
  previewFeatures = [] // No preview features needed for GA features!
}

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  url      = env("DATABASE_URL")
}

// Models
model User {
  id        String   @id @default(cuid())
  email     String   @unique
  name      String?
  password  String   // Use omit to exclude from queries
  posts     Post[]
  profile   Profile?
  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt

  @@index([email])
}

model Profile {
  id     String @id @default(cuid())
  bio    String?
  avatar String?
  userId String @unique
  user   User   @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
}

model Post {
  id        String   @id @default(cuid())
  title     String
  content   String?
  published Boolean  @default(false)
  authorId  String
  author    User     @relation(fields: [authorId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  tags      Tag[]
  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt

  @@index([authorId])
  @@index([published])
}

model Tag {
  id    String @id @default(cuid())
  name  String @unique
  posts Post[]
}
```

### Client Initialization
```typescript
// lib/db.ts
import { PrismaClient } from '@prisma/client'

const globalForPrisma = globalThis as unknown as {
  prisma: PrismaClient | undefined
}

export const prisma =
  globalForPrisma.prisma ??
  new PrismaClient({
    log: process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development' ? ['query', 'error', 'warn'] : ['error'],
  })

if (process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production') globalForPrisma.prisma = prisma
```

## New Features (2025)

### Omit API (GA - Most Requested Feature!)
```typescript
import { Prisma } from '@prisma/client'

// Exclude password from all user queries
const userWithoutPassword = Prisma.validator<Prisma.UserDefaultArgs>()({
  omit: {
    password: true,
  },
})

// Use in queries
const user = await prisma.user.findUnique({
  where: { id: '123' },
  omit: {
    password: true, // Password excluded from result
  },
})

// Global omit configuration
const prisma = new PrismaClient({
  omit: {
    user: {
      password: true, // Always exclude password
    },
  },
})

// Override global omit when needed
const userWithPassword = await prisma.user.findUnique({
  where: { id: '123' },
  omit: {
    password: false, // Include password this time
  },
})
```

### Multi-schema Support (GA)
```prisma
// schema.prisma
generator client {
  provider        = "prisma-client-js"
}

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  url      = env("DATABASE_URL")
  schemas  = ["public", "auth", "analytics"]
}

model User {
  id    String @id @default(cuid())
  email String @unique

  @@schema("auth")
}

model Post {
  id      String @id @default(cuid())
  title   String

  @@schema("public")
}

model Event {
  id        String   @id @default(cuid())
  action    String
  timestamp DateTime @default(now())

  @@schema("analytics")
}
```

### Auto-generated ULIDs
```prisma
model User {
  id String @id @default(ulid()) // ULID instead of UUID
  // ULIDs are sortable, URL-safe, and more compact
}
```

### Sharding Support (@shardKey)
```prisma
// For PlanetScale sharding
model User {
  id         String @id
  tenantId   String @shardKey
  email      String

  @@index([tenantId, email])
}
```

### updateManyAndReturn (2025)
```typescript
// Update multiple records and get them back
const updatedPosts = await prisma.post.updateManyAndReturn({
  where: {
    published: false,
  },
  data: {
    published: true,
  },
})

// updatedPosts contains all updated records
console.log(`Published ${updatedPosts.length} posts`)
```

### JSON Fields in SQLite (2025)
```prisma
// Now supported in SQLite!
model Settings {
  id       String @id @default(cuid())
  config   Json   // JSON field in SQLite
  metadata Json?
}
```

## CRUD Operations

### Create
```typescript
// Create single record
const user = await prisma.user.create({
  data: {
    email: 'alice@example.com',
    name: 'Alice',
    password: await hash('password123'),
  },
  omit: {
    password: true, // Exclude from return
  },
})

// Create with relations
const userWithProfile = await prisma.user.create({
  data: {
    email: 'bob@example.com',
    name: 'Bob',
    password: await hash('password123'),
    profile: {
      create: {
        bio: 'Software developer',
        avatar: 'https://example.com/avatar.jpg',
      },
    },
  },
  include: {
    profile: true,
  },
  omit: {
    password: true,
  },
})

// Bulk create
const users = await prisma.user.createMany({
  data: [
    { email: 'user1@example.com', name: 'User 1', password: 'hash1' },
    { email: 'user2@example.com', name: 'User 2', password: 'hash2' },
  ],
  skipDuplicates: true,
})
```

### Read
```typescript
// Find unique
const user = await prisma.user.findUnique({
  where: { email: 'alice@example.com' },
  include: {
    posts: {
      where: { published: true },
      orderBy: { createdAt: 'desc' },
    },
    profile: true,
  },
  omit: { password: true },
})

// Find many with filters
const publishedPosts = await prisma.post.findMany({
  where: {
    published: true,
    author: {
      email: { contains: '@example.com' },
    },
  },
  include: {
    author: {
      omit: { password: true },
    },
    tags: true,
  },
  orderBy: {
    createdAt: 'desc',
  },
  take: 10,
  skip: 0,
})

// Count
const postCount = await prisma.post.count({
  where: { published: true },
})

// Aggregate
const stats = await prisma.post.aggregate({
  _count: true,
  _avg: { id: true },
  where: { published: true },
})
```

### Update
```typescript
// Update single
const updatedUser = await prisma.user.update({
  where: { id: '123' },
  data: {
    name: 'Alice Updated',
  },
  omit: { password: true },
})

// Update many and return (2025 feature)
const publishedPosts = await prisma.post.updateManyAndReturn({
  where: { published: false },
  data: { published: true },
})

// Upsert
const user = await prisma.user.upsert({
  where: { email: 'alice@example.com' },
  update: { name: 'Alice Updated' },
  create: {
    email: 'alice@example.com',
    name: 'Alice',
    password: await hash('password'),
  },
  omit: { password: true },
})
```

### Delete
```typescript
// Delete single
await prisma.user.delete({
  where: { id: '123' },
})

// Delete many
await prisma.post.deleteMany({
  where: {
    published: false,
    createdAt: {
      lt: new Date('2024-01-01'),
    },
  },
})
```

## Transactions

### Interactive Transactions
```typescript
await prisma.$transaction(async (tx) => {
  const user = await tx.user.create({
    data: {
      email: 'alice@example.com',
      name: 'Alice',
      password: await hash('password'),
    },
  })

  await tx.profile.create({
    data: {
      userId: user.id,
      bio: 'New user',
    },
  })

  await tx.post.create({
    data: {
      title: 'First post',
      authorId: user.id,
    },
  })
})
```

### Sequential Operations
```typescript
const [deletedPosts, createdPost] = await prisma.$transaction([
  prisma.post.deleteMany({ where: { published: false } }),
  prisma.post.create({
    data: {
      title: 'New Post',
      authorId: 'user-123',
    },
  }),
])
```

## Advanced Queries

### Filtering
```typescript
// Complex where conditions
const posts = await prisma.post.findMany({
  where: {
    AND: [
      { published: true },
      {
        OR: [
          { title: { contains: 'Prisma' } },
          { content: { contains: 'Prisma' } },
        ],
      },
    ],
    author: {
      email: { endsWith: '@example.com' },
    },
    createdAt: {
      gte: new Date('2024-01-01'),
      lt: new Date('2025-01-01'),
    },
  },
})
```

### Pagination
```typescript
// Cursor-based pagination
const posts = await prisma.post.findMany({
  take: 10,
  skip: 1, // Skip cursor itself
  cursor: {
    id: lastPostId,
  },
  orderBy: {
    createdAt: 'desc',
  },
})

// Offset-based pagination
const page = 2
const pageSize = 10
const posts = await prisma.post.findMany({
  skip: (page - 1) * pageSize,
  take: pageSize,
  orderBy: { createdAt: 'desc' },
})
```

### Relations
```typescript
// Nested reads
const user = await prisma.user.findUnique({
  where: { id: '123' },
  include: {
    posts: {
      include: {
        tags: true,
      },
    },
    profile: true,
  },
  omit: { password: true },
})

// Nested writes
const post = await prisma.post.create({
  data: {
    title: 'New Post',
    author: {
      connect: { id: 'user-123' },
    },
    tags: {
      connectOrCreate: [
        {
          where: { name: 'typescript' },
          create: { name: 'typescript' },
        },
      ],
    },
  },
})
```

## Migrations

### Development Workflow
```bash
# Create and apply migration
npx prisma migrate dev --name add_user_role

# Reset database (development only!)
npx prisma migrate reset

# Generate Prisma Client
npx prisma generate
```

### Production Deployment
```bash
# Apply pending migrations
npx prisma migrate deploy

# Check migration status
npx prisma migrate status
```

## Best Practices (2025)

1. **Use omit API** - Exclude sensitive fields like passwords globally
2. **Leverage Rust-free benefits** - Smaller bundles, faster queries
3. **Use ULIDs over UUIDs** - Better sortability and compactness
4. **Multi-schema organization** - Separate concerns with schemas
5. **updateManyAndReturn** - Get updated records in bulk operations
6. **Connection pooling** - Use PgBouncer or similar in production
7. **Type safety** - Use Prisma.validator for type-safe configurations
8. **Soft deletes** - Add deletedAt field instead of hard deletes
9. **Indexes** - Add @@index for frequently queried fields
10. **Cascading deletes** - Use onDelete: Cascade for related data
11. **Transaction isolation** - Use $transaction for atomic operations
12. **Pagination** - Prefer cursor-based over offset for large datasets
13. **Prisma Postgres** - Use for local development
14. **VS Code extension** - Visual database management
15. **Ask AI** - Use integrated AI for help
